Project Mu: return each session to Mu when the browser closes

Ichi-go ichi-e: nothing a session leaves behind should outlive it.

  * Cookies and site data (localStorage, IndexedDB, service workers, ...)
    default to "session only": they live in memory for the session and are
    deleted on exit. This is the "Delete data sites have saved when you close
    all windows" setting (policy DefaultCookiesSetting = 4), so users can still
    keep chosen sites signed in via Settings > Site settings.
  * The ClearBrowsingDataOnExitList pref now defaults to browsing history,
    download history and cached images/files. ChromeBrowsingDataLifetimeManager
    deletes these when the profile shuts down, and retries on the next start
    if the browser crashed. Deletion only runs while browser sign-in is
    disabled (0003 makes that the default), so synced data is never wiped.

Passwords, autofill data and site permissions are kept: users save those
deliberately.

